Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight Private Permit Bridge P0 Threat Review

@ [threat_review_uuid] b1694a41-1723-4dfd-88ad-757c90c0ee4f
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 750fbbb5-f72f-4816-882f-d8b0ebf1acc7

& [Threats]
  + constructing admission from correspondence alone work language publication fixture or inferred consent
  + exposing admission bridge issuer or permit through pub use binary CLI environment feature callback trait object or alternate entry
  + cloning serializing defaulting persisting logging recovering or returning admission or permit
  + minting before full pure validation minting twice moving permit after another operation or retrying after runner fault
  + substituting activation runner producer controller plan target executable argv time stream process or effect coordinates
  + accepting a returned run without canonical reparse existing receipt validation and effect conservation
  + laundering provider-unavailable post-consumption fault or receipt refusal into retry repair fallback or success

& [Controls]
  + module and item crate-private visibility no public re-export no production admission constructor and private fields
  + Rust non-Clone ownership FnOnce execution and one lexical issue-then-move sequence
  + exact lineage and input replay before mint plus exact issuer validation at the runner boundary
  + terminal typed projection after issuance with no capability-bearing return and no loop
  + static source gates compile-time visibility expectations provider-free unit adversaries and independent formation replay

& [Residual]
  + same-crate code changes could deliberately widen visibility or add construction; current static gates detect only the reviewed tree and must be rerun on every change
  + production identity custody trusted time revocation replay prevention and invocation evidence remain unsolved until separately governed live initiation
